WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.690
The real reason 4-20 has become a stoner holiday
is a little hazy, but one thing's for sure:

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:10.559
It's blazed its way into popular culture something
fierce, inspiring every nerd with a Bob Marley

00:00:10.559 --> 00:00:14.379
poster and a stack of Taco Bell coupons to
call out sick that day on account of their

00:00:14.379 --> 00:00:15.999
"sore throat."

00:00:15.999 --> 00:00:20.529
So it comes as no surprise that movie studios,
record labels, and even game developers would

00:00:20.529 --> 00:00:22.500
take advantage of its unofficial festivities.

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:28.200
"If he ain't back in 10 minutes, we're calling
Dominoes."

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:34.079
Whether you're a diehard gamer or a dedicated
music-lover, be sure to mark April 20th, 2018

00:00:34.079 --> 00:00:37.250
on your calendar, because there's a ton of
cool new stuff coming out that day.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:42.260
Here are some of the most smokin' releases
you can't afford to miss this 4-20.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:43.720
Super Troopers 2

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:48.239
The long-gestating sequel to the 2001 cult
comedy Super Troopers is finally coming to

00:00:48.239 --> 00:00:52.829
theaters this year, after a successful Indiegogo
campaign made a second outing for everyone's

00:00:52.829 --> 00:00:55.129
favorite Vermont state troopers possible.

00:00:55.129 --> 00:00:59.390
Written by and starring comedy troupe Broken
Lizard, the movie will pit Thorny, Foster,

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:04.290
Mac, Rabbit, and Farva against a group of
Canadian Mounties after a small slice of Canada

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:06.880
is found to actually be on U.S. soil.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:10.700
By the time the film drops it will have been
almost two decades since the Broken Lizard

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:14.890
guys first appeared as the outrageous law
enforcement unit, though it appears that not

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:17.520
a lot has changed for the characters in that
time.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.570
Broken Lizard founding member Steve Lemme
told Vermont newspaper Seven Days:

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:25.689
"Well, we do all have cellphones in this movie
[...] But otherwise, it seems like time has

00:01:25.689 --> 00:01:28.420
stood still for these state troopers."

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:29.770
Rampage

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:33.280
On the surface, Rampage doesn't look like
your typical 4-20 release.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:37.860
But one of glimpse the trailer and the logic
becomes clear — this Dwayne Johnson blockbuster

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:41.590
looks like the product of an especially smokey
brainstorming session.

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:45.290
The flick is actually based on a series of
video games in which the player has to take

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:49.799
control of a giant beast and destroy an entire
city before the military takes you down.

00:01:49.799 --> 00:01:52.340
But this… this is something different.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:57.159
The former WWE superstar has faced off against
some fearsome opponents in his time, but this

00:01:57.159 --> 00:02:02.399
April we'll get to see how the Rock fares
against a genetically modified 30-foot wolf.

00:02:02.399 --> 00:02:05.930
Don't expect him to be wrestling with huge
animals, however — he's actually on their

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:06.930
side.

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:10.420
Sounds like a typical Tuesday night for everybody's
favorite hard-hitting heavyweight!

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:14.720
[Grunting]

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:21.590
God of War

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:25.860
The hotly anticipated God of War is finally
just around the corner.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:29.930
Not only will the latest entry in the action
series see brand new gameplay elements like

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:35.030
an emphasis on exploration, but it'll boast
a brand new environment for players to traverse.

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:39.650
While previous installments have all been
based around Greek Mythology, this time out,

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:43.780
Kratos and his son Atreus will be kicking
butt in a world of Norse myth instead.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:47.490
The game's writer and director Cory Barlog
is confident that fans will dig the new God

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:49.920
of War when it hits shelves on 4-20.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.120
On his PlayStation Blog, Barlog wrote,

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:56.180
"First, let me say that this is my favorite
release day of my entire career.

00:02:56.180 --> 00:03:00.640
If I live to be 100, I do not think I will
be able to top this release day."

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:02.000
Nintendo Labo

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:06.560
The success of Nintendo's Switch cemented
the company's position as the king of party

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:07.570
hardware.

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:11.600
On 4-20, those parties are going to get even
better with the addition of cardboard.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:14.500
Yep, you heard that right: cardboard.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:19.040
The Nintendo Labo is a variety of different
perforated cut-out kits that the user builds

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:20.040
at home.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:24.500
These 'Toy-Cons,' as Nintendo is calling them,
are able to interact with the game's software.

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:29.150
It might seem like a bizarre concept, but
according to Nintendo director Shinya Takahashi,

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:31.790
playing with cardboard is quite common for
Japanese kids.

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:36.270
"It's not so far-fetched if you consider how
familiar the material is, at least to Japanese

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:40.670
people who, from a young age, use it for play
and as a material for creating things such

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:42.240
as fancy crafts."

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:46.570
Whether western gamers will warm up to the
idea is anybody's guess, as many will likely

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:48.290
be put off by the price tag.

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:54.170
The variety kit and the robot kit retail at
$69.99 and $79.99, respectively.

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:56.780
But can you really put a price on this much
fun?

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:58.640
Back to the Future manga

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:02.680
Hollywood has been trying — and failing
— to successfully adapt Japanese properties

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:07.770
for western audiences for years now, but rarely
does that relationship go the other way.

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:11.760
On 4-20, we're going to get the chance to
see what something truly American looks like

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:15.070
through a Japanese lens — and not just any
old lens.

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:19.060
Yusuke Murata, the
illustrator who adapted popular webcomic One-Punch

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:23.650
Man into a full-fledged manga, announced his
own Back to the Future project during a recent

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:25.310
promotional event in Tokyo.

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:29.400
The film's screenwriter Bob Gale is acting
as a supervisor on the project, which will

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:34.630
reportedly expand on the story of Marty McFly
with material not seen in the original trilogy.

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:38.960
The first images show just how great a job
Murata's done at capturing Marty and the rest

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.900
of the cast, especially Christopher Lloyd's
Doc Brown.

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:45.680
Thankfully for those of us living outside
Japan, Murata's Back to the Future, which

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:50.850
will be titled BTTF, will be collected and
published on 4-20.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:52.660
Sting and Shaggy album

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:56.160
When Sting appeared at the Grammys earlier
this year, those in attendance were enjoying

00:04:56.160 --> 00:05:00.450
a performance of his classic "Englishman in
New York" when they got a surprise : Shaggy,

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:04.570
who changed the lyrics to "Jamaican in New
York" and debuted a snippet of the pair's

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.230
first single, "Don't Make Me Wait."

00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:10.040
At the end of the performance, the "It Wasn't
Me" singer announced that the two were releasing

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:13.190
a joint, Caribbean-inspired album on 4-20.

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:16.400
According to Billboard, the two musicians
immediately hit it off during a fundraiser

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:19.220
thanks in part to their mutual love for Jamaica.

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:21.030
Sting opened up about their friendship, saying,

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:22.180
"We just had a rapport.

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:24.791
[...] In the early '80s, I was in Jamaica
a lot.

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:26.470
I wrote 'Every Breath You Take' in Jamaica.

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:31.140
So Jamaica was a kind of refuge and obviously
a great influence on my own musical DNA with

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.690
reggae, so I felt I owed a debt to Jamaica."

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:37.780
If "Don't Make Me Wait" is any indication,
we'd say Sting's paid off his debts to Shaggy's

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:41.070
Caribbean homeland — and we're all richer
for it.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.080
New A Perfect Circle album

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:47.190
Alternative rock supergroup A Perfect Circle
is back with a brand new album this April,

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:50.770
and it'll be their first major release in
14 years.

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:54.900
On 4-20, their fourth album, Eat the Elephant,
will hit record stores nationwide.

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:58.750
A Perfect Circle founder and vocalist Maynard
James Keenan explained the decision to release

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:01.610
their fourth studio album on 4-20, telling
AXS,

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:05.380
"The 20th of April is [British singer-songwriter]
Carina Round's birthday.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:08.920
She is a dear friend who is extremely difficult
to shop for.

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:09.920
Pressure off.

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:13.750
Of course, I must also note that the potheads
are gonna be thrilled that this album comes

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:15.130
out on 4-20.

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:19.660
May it serve as a glorious soundtrack to accompany
all of the giggling and vexing sounds of nibbling

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:20.750
and snacking.

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:22.960
Fingers crossed, Cheech and Chong will be
proud."

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:25.360
Music, munchies, and mellowing out?

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:27.860
We think the iconic duo would approve.

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:35.640
"Mellow… mellow… mellow… yeah."

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:37.320
Thanks for watching!

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:39.410
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:41.490
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

